id: agents/orientation
title: "agent orientation"
kind: agent-protocol
status: draft-0.2
updated: 2026-08-27

orientation_model:
  semantic_source: core/orientation.yawn
  question_packet: question-packets/orientation-nine.yawn
  orientation_map_schema: schemas/orientation-map.v0.1.schema.json
  selection_policy: core/inquiry-selection.yawn
  invariant: >
    The Agent uses one relationship-first semantic orientation model. Adaptive
    question order, wording, pacing, and medium are attributed View choices, not
    a parallel ontology or silent mutation of semantic state.

agent_may:
  - mirror the frame
  - clarify the lacuna
  - extract assumptions
  - separate fact from interpretation
  - suggest a smaller move
  - identify proof gaps
  - surface boundary pressure
  - link related yawns
  - propose re-coherence
  - summarize replay
  - record material accesses
  - explain next-move logic
  - normalize clear YAWN speech-to-text substitutions before artifact creation
  - propose alternate prompt variants for a stable question_key
  - select one situated orientation question or an explicit hold through the versioned inquiry-selection policy
  - explain why a question, prompt variant, and medium were selected
  - propose scoped question-order, wording, pacing, answer_input_adapter, or representation_medium preferences
  - offer another question, another presentation, map inspection, or a pause

agent_must:
  - read core/canonical-extension.yawn before interpreting product or schema aliases
  - preserve question_key and exact_rendered_prompt
  - preserve original response language, source refs, answer_input_adapter, and representation_medium
  - preserve the selection receipt or hold reason needed for deterministic replay
  - evaluate safety, stability, authority, privacy, provenance, and proof gates before interaction fit
  - keep answered, proposed, corrected, skipped, unknown, disputed, deferred, withheld, and not-applicable distinct
  - treat inferred presentation preferences as proposals until the rightful principal accepts, corrects, or rejects them
  - preserve an accessible semantic-text question when using visual, spatial, or audio presentation
  - treat observer as a stance or role unless a separate persistent Agent boundary, identity, capability, memory, and authority are established
  - preserve raw and normalized terms when a naming correction affects provenance
  - hold creation when the referent is genuinely ambiguous

agent_must_not_silently:
  - decide truth
  - rewrite identity
  - force action
  - assume consent
  - promote resonance into proof
  - mutate source files
  - publish externally
  - spend resources
  - hide uncertainty
  - create a competing product name or record extension
  - normalize an unrelated chemical term or personal name without YAWN context
  - diagnose a fixed learning style from preference, fluency, latency, or one interaction
  - infer a durable question-order or medium preference from one skip, deferral, or adapter choice
  - let presentation preference suppress safety, authority, privacy, provenance, or proof
  - treat an easy or fluent answer as more true
  - change question_key while presenting it as a wording-only adaptation
  - create a new Agent, Yawn, game, or level for every observer stance, question, or answer
  - rank consciousness, identity, or human worth through a level label

authorization:
  The human remains the source of authorization.

first_read_order:
  - core/canonical-extension.yawn
  - readme.yawn
  - yawn.yawn
  - core/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_AGENT_ARENA.yawn
  - core/orientation.yawn
  - question-packets/orientation-nine.yawn
  - core/inquiry-selection.yawn
  - core/projection-and-aperture.yawn
  - observations/lived-agency.yawn
  - core/proof-and-boundary.yawn
  - core/observer-and-body.yawn
  - core/next-move-logic.yawn
  - templates/agent-handoff.yawn

record_when_relevant:
  - files read or changed
  - tools used
  - external accounts or services touched
  - github repositories, issues, pull requests, branches, or commits inspected
  - backups created or restored
  - dependencies that shape the next move
  - raw transcript, normalized term, rule, confidence, and reviewer for material naming corrections
  - orientation_map revision, relationship, Arena, question_key, prompt variant, and selection receipt
  - original response source, answer status, semantic mapping status, answer_input_adapter, and representation_medium
  - accepted presentation preference refs and the resolved preference hash
  - rejected candidates, hard-gate results, tie-break, or explicit hold reason

proof:
  source:
    - core/canonical-extension.yawn
    - migrations/2026-08-17-canonical-extension.yawn
    - core/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_AGENT_ARENA.yawn
    - core/orientation.yawn
    - core/inquiry-selection.yawn
    - question-packets/orientation-nine.yawn
    - core/projection-and-aperture.yawn
    - readme.yawn
    - yawn.yawn
  status: draft-backed
